<title>UK: BP slips amid talk of switching.</title>
<headline>BP slips amid talk of switching.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Petroleum slipped on Tuesday amid talk of switching out of the shares into Shell Transport, traders said.</p>
<p>By 0838 GMT, BP shares were down 7p to 688-1/2p on trading volume of 2.6 million. They were among the most actively traded shares in London. Shares in Shell, meanwhile, were up 3p to 1032p.  </p>
<p>There was also talk of one large institution sharply reducing a previously overweight position in BP, a market maker said.</p>
<p>-- Debra Sherman, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
